@* M4.S7 — bypass <Router>/<Routes> (which trips an AOT struct-copy bug
   in StaticHtmlRenderer.RenderAttributes when reading reference-typed
   attribute values like NotFoundPage Type / AppAssembly). Render Counter
   inline. blazor.web.js still picks up the <!--Blazor:server--> markers
   emitted by BlazorMarkerMiddleware and hydrates this component over the
   SignalR Long Polling transport. *@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    <title>Blazor Server on IC — Counter</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="lib/bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="app.css" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="favicon.png" />
    <HeadOutlet />
</head>

<body style="font-family: system-ui; max-width: 720px; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem;">
    <h1 style="color: #2563eb;">Blazor Server on IC</h1>
    <p>Counter rendered server-side. Click events ride <strong>SignalR Long Polling</strong> over the canister's HTTP gateway — no WebSocket, no external services.</p>

    <Counter />

    <hr />
    <small>Server-rendered shell + <code>blazor.web.js</code> from the asset canister. SignalR transport is pinned to <code>HttpTransportType.LongPolling</code> (value 4) so the client never tries WebSocket. <code>/_blazor/negotiate</code>, <code>/_blazor</code> POST (send), and <code>/_blazor</code> GET (poll) are all routed to the backend canister's <code>http_request_update</code>.</small>

    <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js" autostart="false"></script>
    <script>
      // HttpTransportType: 1=WebSockets, 2=ServerSentEvents, 4=LongPolling.
      // Pinning to 4 because canisters can't host real WebSockets; SSE
      // would require IcServer to honor streaming_strategy callbacks
      // (separate work item).
      Blazor.start({
        circuit: {
          configureSignalR: builder => {
            builder.withUrl('/_blazor', { transport: 4 });
          }
        }
      });
    </script>
</body>

</html>
